{"id":104,"text":"Two monks were travelling together when they reached a shallow river. A young woman in an elegant dress stood on the bank, unable to cross without ruining her clothes and, worse, losing her footing in the current.\n\nWithout a word, the older monk lifted her onto his shoulders, carried her across and set her down gently on the other side. She thanked him warmly, and the monks continued on their way.\n\nThe younger monk, however, grew increasingly uneasy. They had been taught to avoid contact with women, and he could not understand his companion’s behaviour. For an hour, he walked in silence, his irritation growing with every step.\n\nFinally, he could bear it no longer. “How could you do that?” he burst out. “You broke our vows! You carried that woman as if it were nothing!”\n\nThe older monk looked at him calmly. “I left her by the river two hours ago,” he said. “Are you still carrying her?”\n\nThe younger monk fell silent. He suddenly realised that while his companion had done a simple act of kindness and moved on, he himself had spent two hours turning the moment over in his mind, building resentment out of a single gesture.\n\nThey walked on without speaking, but the younger monk’s step had become lighter.\n\nMoral: Don’t carry yesterday’s moments into today. Let them go.","tr":null,"gl":{"two":"ikki","monks":"rohiblar","were":"edi(lar)","travelling":"sayohat","together":"birga","when":"qachon; -ganda","they":"ular","reached":"yetdi","a":"bir (noaniq artikl)","shallow":"sayoz","river":"daryo","young":"yosh","woman":"ayol","in":"ichida, -da","an":"bir (noaniq artikl)","elegant":"nafis","dress":"ko'ylak","stood":"turdi","on":"ustida, -da","the":"(aniq artikl)","bank":"bank; qirg'oq","unable":"qodir emas","to":"-ga; uchun","cross":"kesib o'tmoq","without":"-siz","ruining":"buzib","her":"uni; uning (ayol)","clothes":"kiyimlar","and":"va","worse":"yomonroq","losing":"yutqazayotgan","footing":"oyoq tirash joyi","current":"oqim","word":"so'z","older":